3
00:00:50.842 --> 00:00:53.384
It comes down to one question.

4
00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.678
Will you survive high school?

5
00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:56.680
Will I survive?

6
00:00:57.682 --> 00:00:59.852
'Cause I know too
many people who didn't.

7
00:01:04.981 --> 00:01:07.651
We have said too many goodbyes.

8
00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.775
grieved too long.

9
00:01:12.655 --> 00:01:17.075
Liberty High has endured
enough traumas and tragedy.

10
00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:20.117
and the loss of another
classmate senior year...

11
00:01:21.331 --> 00:01:24.213
is more than children
should be asked to bear.

12
00:01:24.215 --> 00:01:27.001
but Liberty is not alone.

13
00:01:27.879 --> 00:01:32.799
Too many high schools today are
forced to reckon with tragedy.

14
00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:36.803
Too many of our young people
are not making it to graduation.

15
00:01:36.805 --> 00:01:40.848
and we are doing too
little to make change.

16
00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:45.770
And we must ask not only
how we can make change.

17
00:01:46.648 --> 00:01:50.488
but what we have done to
shape their world this way.

18
00:01:51.569 --> 00:01:54.109
How are we responsible?

19
00:01:57.534 --> 00:02:00.164
What burdens are we
placing on our young people?

20
00:02:02.205 --> 00:02:04.415
What tools are we keeping from them?

21
00:02:07.418 --> 00:02:08.838
How did we get here...

22
00:02:10.588 --> 00:02:11.588
again?

23
00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:14.242
What? What the...

24
00:03:15.987 --> 00:03:16.987
Justin?

25
00:03:17.947 --> 00:03:18.987
Put your clothes on.

26
00:03:19.908 --> 00:03:20.908
We gotta go.

27
00:03:22.744 --> 00:03:24.702
Where are we going?

28
00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:27.214
Monty. he's still alive.

29
00:03:50.104 --> 00:03:51.104
What?

30
00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:54.106
What the fuck do you want?

31
00:03:54.108 --> 00:03:56.238
Monty. we're sorry.

32
00:03:58.029 --> 00:04:00.069
We didn't think this
would happen. We thought...

33
00:04:00.823 --> 00:04:03.157
I mean. we thought you were dead.

34
00:04:03.159 --> 00:04:06.528
- We didn't think that...
- You wanted to clear your name?

35
00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:08.114
So you set me up for murder?

36
00:04:08.116 --> 00:04:09.877
We were trying to protect someone else.

37
00:04:09.879 --> 00:04:11.276
We thought you were gone.

38
00:04:12.293 --> 00:04:14.293
They carried me out like I was.

39
00:04:14.295 --> 00:04:18.085
but. you know. 200 stitches and
a few surgeries. and here I am.

40
00:04:18.967 --> 00:04:21.884
- We can work this out.
- No. we can't fucking work it out!

41
00:04:21.886 --> 00:04:24.454
I'm going away for life. What
the fuck are we going to work out?

42
00:04:24.456 --> 00:04:26.973
Well. there'll be a trial.
and we can testify...

43
00:04:26.975 --> 00:04:30.265
Guys like me. they don't get
trials. And what about Bryce?

44
00:04:31.145 --> 00:04:32.225
What about Bryce?

45
00:04:33.022 --> 00:04:35.815
- How does he get justice?
- Bryce hurt a lot of people.

46
00:04:35.817 --> 00:04:37.900
Yeah. and you're no better than he is.

47
00:04:37.902 --> 00:04:40.987
You fuck with whoever you
want. ruin people's lives.

48
00:04:40.989 --> 00:04:43.364
Bryce was a fucking rapist.

49
00:04:43.366 --> 00:04:44.446
and so were you.

50
00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.632
I've been having these... bad dreams.

51
00:05:02.719 --> 00:05:04.135
like. every night.

52
00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:10.933
It's pretty messed up. but
I'm good at hiding shit. so...

53
00:05:10.935 --> 00:05:13.561
I don't think my parents have noticed.

54
00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:19.211
Clay. honey. um. you sure you
don't want to come with us

55
00:05:19.213 --> 00:05:21.360
to the facility today?

56
00:05:21.362 --> 00:05:22.362
Might be fun.

57
00:05:23.239 --> 00:05:26.239
When is anything called a
facility ever fun?

58
00:05:27.285 --> 00:05:28.995
- Justin might like to see you.
- Mm.

59
00:05:29.746 --> 00:05:30.906
I'll see him at home...

60
00:05:31.748 --> 00:05:32.748
at the party.

61
00:05:36.627 --> 00:05:40.257
Clay. your. um. first-semester
grades came in yesterday.

62
00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:44.717
- How do you have my grades?
- The school email.

63
00:05:44.719 --> 00:05:45.719
As always.

64
00:05:48.222 --> 00:05:49.222
Oh.

65
00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:52.017
Right.

66
00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:54.353
I didn't...

67
00:05:55.563 --> 00:05:58.147
I didn't do too well on my finals.

68
00:05:58.149 --> 00:06:01.567
- Which is understandable.
- We're going to talk to the school.

69
00:06:01.569 --> 00:06:02.985
- No!
- We're going to talk to them

70
00:06:02.987 --> 00:06:06.739
about some allowances for
what you've been through.

71
00:06:06.741 --> 00:06:08.831
but... Clay.

72
00:06:09.911 --> 00:06:11.831
you need to be thinking about college.

73
00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:16.123
Have you finished your apps?

74
00:06:16.125 --> 00:06:17.802
We just want you

75
00:06:17.804 --> 00:06:19.627
to feel like you can
come to us for anything.

76
00:06:19.629 --> 00:06:21.962
but if you don't feel like you
can come to us for anything.

77
00:06:21.964 --> 00:06:23.613
then I think we need to start thinking

78
00:06:23.615 --> 00:06:25.508
about starting up again with Dr. Ellman.

79
00:06:28.179 --> 00:06:29.179
Shit!

80
00:06:30.765 --> 00:06:31.765
Sorry.

81
00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:37.064
So. Clay. what do you think?

82
00:06:38.064 --> 00:06:39.897
About what?

83
00:06:39.899 --> 00:06:41.649
About seeing Dr. Ellman.

84
00:06:44.821 --> 00:06:45.821
Um...

85
00:06:47.532 --> 00:06:48.622
I don't know.

86
00:07:07.802 --> 00:07:10.142
Here's the thing. I'm basically okay.

87
00:07:15.435 --> 00:07:17.191
I mean. as okay as you can be

88
00:07:17.193 --> 00:07:19.353
a month out from
being in jail for murder.

89
00:07:23.818 --> 00:07:24.818
Hey. Tyler.

90
00:07:29.907 --> 00:07:30.907
What?

91
00:07:32.034 --> 00:07:33.164
Did they say why?

92
00:07:36.414 --> 00:07:37.997
Okay. hey. just listen.

93
00:07:37.999 --> 00:07:41.589
Just calm down. breathe. sit tight.
and give me a few minutes.

94
00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:46.715
But then a friend needed me.
and it was like I was alive again.

95
00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:52.306
My girlfriend. no.

96
00:07:53.973 --> 00:07:55.313
She doesn't need me.

97
00:07:56.184 --> 00:08:00.603
Well. I think she loves me. or
at least she likes me. I think.

98
00:08:00.605 --> 00:08:01.605
Hey!

99
00:08:02.982 --> 00:08:04.899
Hey. you're early.

100
00:08:04.901 --> 00:08:06.321
Nice to see you as well.

101
00:08:08.404 --> 00:08:10.114
- What is it?
- I was...

102
00:08:10.865 --> 00:08:13.866
I was hoping we could talk about...

103
00:08:13.868 --> 00:08:14.950
us and everything.

104
00:08:14.952 --> 00:08:16.076
Okay. I gotta go.

105
00:08:16.078 --> 00:08:18.120
I... I'm... Tyler got called in

106
00:08:18.122 --> 00:08:19.788
- to talk to the sheriff.
- What the fuck?

107
00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:22.249
He's alone at home. His parents
don't know. I gotta drive him.

108
00:08:22.251 --> 00:08:24.293
- Does he think it's about Bryce?
- He doesn't know.

109
00:08:24.295 --> 00:08:25.544
- I'm coming with you.
- No.

110
00:08:25.546 --> 00:08:28.088
You should stay and help
Jess set up for the party.

111
00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:29.673
or she'll freak out.

112
00:08:29.675 --> 00:08:31.342
Okay. are you freaking out?

113
00:08:31.344 --> 00:08:32.843
No. I'm good. I'm...

114
00:08:32.845 --> 00:08:34.803
- I'm totally good.
- Clay. look at me.

115
00:08:34.805 --> 00:08:36.055
Look at me. Clay.

116
00:08:36.891 --> 00:08:39.731
- This will be fine.
- Yeah. No. I know. I got this.

117
00:08:48.945 --> 00:08:51.403
Why do I take care of my friends?

118
00:08:51.405 --> 00:08:53.781
Because they need me.

119
00:08:53.783 --> 00:08:56.575
All right. just be calm
so you can think clearly.

120
00:08:56.577 --> 00:09:00.496
If it gets rough. you stop them.
ask for a lawyer. and call me.

121
00:09:00.498 --> 00:09:02.081
All right. Yeah. got it.

122
00:09:04.502 --> 00:09:05.876
Will you wait?

123
00:09:05.878 --> 00:09:06.878
Of course.

124
00:09:07.922 --> 00:09:08.922
Okay.

125
00:09:15.429 --> 00:09:17.009
Man. I thought this was over.

126
00:09:18.933 --> 00:09:20.266
Me too.

127
00:09:20.268 --> 00:09:22.768
Clay. why is this happening now?

128
00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:23.850
I'm not sure...

129
00:09:24.897 --> 00:09:27.527
but it's gonna be fine. okay?

130
00:09:29.151 --> 00:09:30.531
You trust me. right?

131
00:09:33.239 --> 00:09:34.239
Always.

132
00:09:38.077 --> 00:09:41.117
Okay.

133
00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:49.760
It's nothing in particular.
It's just high school now-a-days.

134
00:09:50.673 --> 00:09:54.973
You can never let your guard down
because it never fucking ends.

135
00:09:57.305 --> 00:09:59.056
And friends have to rely on each other.

136
00:09:59.058 --> 00:10:01.181
or bad shit might happen.

137
00:10:01.183 --> 00:10:03.809
It smells like an ass
wore shoes in here.

138
00:10:03.811 --> 00:10:06.979
Like. ass shoes on a dead animal.

139
00:10:06.981 --> 00:10:08.522
Is Clay all right?

140
00:10:08.524 --> 00:10:10.694
Yeah... Yeah. he's fine.

141
00:10:12.528 --> 00:10:14.069
Stellar.

142
00:10:14.071 --> 00:10:16.371
Do you love him. or are
you just taking care of him?

143
00:10:17.366 --> 00:10:19.992
Uh. don't we take care of
the people that we love?

144
00:10:19.994 --> 00:10:21.914
I mean. he's been going through a lot.

145
00:10:24.123 --> 00:10:26.415
So you haven't told him about Oakland.

146
00:10:26.417 --> 00:10:28.042
Um...

147
00:10:28.044 --> 00:10:29.054
Not yet.

148
00:10:29.837 --> 00:10:31.670
I was meant to tell him today.

149
00:10:31.672 --> 00:10:34.923
but we don't move until
after Christmas. so...

150
00:10:34.925 --> 00:10:36.759
You've known for a week.

151
00:10:36.761 --> 00:10:40.011
and you knew once you told
him. he'd go all Clay cray.

152
00:10:41.307 --> 00:10:42.307
Clay-zy.

153
00:10:43.684 --> 00:10:45.684
- No. I like Clay cray.
- Okay. no.

154
00:10:45.686 --> 00:10:48.686
Look. Honestly. I was gonna
tell him just now. but...

155
00:10:50.232 --> 00:10:52.399
well. he had to take care of something.

156
00:10:52.401 --> 00:10:54.610
- What. something about Justin?
- No.

157
00:10:54.612 --> 00:10:58.072
All's good there. He's still
due home at four. so breathe.

158
00:11:00.201 --> 00:11:01.867
People have been relying on me.

159
00:11:01.869 --> 00:11:04.501
so I gotta. like. be strong and stuff.

160
00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:24.306
And the dreams. and anxiety
and stuff. makes me not strong.

161
00:11:25.726 --> 00:11:27.142
What the fuck?

162
00:11:52.211 --> 00:11:53.211
Hey!

163
00:12:03.097 --> 00:12:04.097
Hey.

164
00:12:05.141 --> 00:12:06.141
Hey.

165
00:12:07.017 --> 00:12:08.726
Hey. are you okay?

166
00:12:08.728 --> 00:12:10.438
Yeah. Fine.

167
00:12:13.482 --> 00:12:14.482
What happened?

168
00:12:15.234 --> 00:12:17.860
They found the guns...

169
00:12:17.862 --> 00:12:18.887
... in the river.

170
00:12:18.889 --> 00:12:19.903
Fuck.

171
00:12:19.905 --> 00:12:22.489
And they couldn't trace
it to anyone at first.

172
00:12:22.491 --> 00:12:26.368
You know. there's no serial
number. no prints. but the bag...

173
00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:28.870
they traced the bag to
the store I bought it from.

174
00:12:30.166 --> 00:12:33.266
But I told them that I bought it.

175
00:12:33.268 --> 00:12:35.002
but that someone else stole it from me.

176
00:12:35.004 --> 00:12:36.837
And they believed you?

177
00:12:36.839 --> 00:12:38.338
Well. Alex's dad was there.

178
00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:40.048
He helped me out.

179
00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:41.842
I think we're okay.

180
00:12:46.015 --> 00:12:48.223
Let's keep this between
you and me for now.

181
00:12:48.225 --> 00:12:49.683
Yeah.

182
00:12:49.685 --> 00:12:52.725
- Yeah?
- Yeah. for sure. Yeah.

183
00:12:53.731 --> 00:12:56.815
I can't tell my friends anything
about what I'm going through

184
00:12:56.817 --> 00:12:59.237
because they count on me to be solid.

185
00:12:59.239 --> 00:13:00.986
Car coming. Justin's here.

186
00:13:00.988 --> 00:13:03.322
Come on. everyone. under
the banner. Let's go.

187
00:13:03.324 --> 00:13:06.658
Jesus Christ. how fucking hard
is it? Under the banner. Let's go.

188
00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:08.290
Hey. fucking smile. okay?

189
00:13:12.082 --> 00:13:13.415
Um...

190
00:13:13.417 --> 00:13:15.209
- Hi.
- Fuck's sake.

191
00:13:15.211 --> 00:13:16.627
- Where's the cake?
- Um...

192
00:13:16.629 --> 00:13:18.504
I still need to get it.

193
00:13:18.506 --> 00:13:20.216
All right. stand down.

194
00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:23.759
Things have been weird lately.

195
00:13:23.761 --> 00:13:25.844
We got busy with finals.
then winter break.

196
00:13:25.846 --> 00:13:28.056
We haven't exactly been hanging out.

197
00:13:31.435 --> 00:13:34.019
He's here! Everyone under
the damn banner. Come on.

198
00:13:34.021 --> 00:13:35.729
Smile!

199
00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:39.358
Welcome home!

200
00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:41.819
Oh. I'm home!

201
00:13:41.821 --> 00:13:44.655
No. I'm just kidding.
It's for Justin. I know.

202
00:13:44.657 --> 00:13:45.932
You're late.

203
00:13:45.934 --> 00:13:46.949
I know.

204
00:13:46.951 --> 00:13:48.371
And are you drunk?

205
00:13:49.745 --> 00:13:50.785
I. uh...

206
00:13:51.747 --> 00:13:52.788
may have pregamed.

207
00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:53.872
Yes.

208
00:13:53.874 --> 00:13:55.290
Oh. my God.

209
00:13:55.292 --> 00:13:57.042
What the fuck is wrong with you?

210
00:13:57.044 --> 00:14:00.629
This is a dry party for a sober person.

211
00:14:00.631 --> 00:14:02.673
Hey. get some mouthwash
or something. Come on.

212
00:14:02.675 --> 00:14:05.634
- Oh. cookies!
- Chili powder. secret ingredient.

213
00:14:05.636 --> 00:14:07.511
Oh. so fucking good.

214
00:14:08.597 --> 00:14:09.847
We're here!

215
00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:13.810
Yeah!

216
00:14:15.604 --> 00:14:16.654
Welcome home!

217
00:14:18.858 --> 00:14:19.858
Yeah.

218
00:14:21.777 --> 00:14:22.777
Hey. um...

219
00:14:23.696 --> 00:14:25.362
welcome home.

220
00:14:25.364 --> 00:14:26.364
Thanks.

221
00:14:28.075 --> 00:14:30.659
Hope you kids brought your appetites.

222
00:14:30.661 --> 00:14:31.661
Dig in!

223
00:14:35.374 --> 00:14:36.424
What's up. man?

224
00:14:38.711 --> 00:14:40.294
Hey. Jess.

225
00:14:40.296 --> 00:14:41.296
Hey.

226
00:14:44.425 --> 00:14:46.255
He seems great. right?

227
00:14:47.887 --> 00:14:49.047
Right.

228
00:14:52.808 --> 00:14:54.057
He's doing fine.

229
00:14:54.059 --> 00:14:57.019
- Let's just talk about it later. okay?
- Are we screwed or not?

230
00:14:57.021 --> 00:15:00.439
I don't think so. but if
people see us whispering.

231
00:15:00.441 --> 00:15:02.399
I don't want to freak everybody out.

232
00:15:02.401 --> 00:15:04.111
What the fuck is up with Tyler?

233
00:15:06.155 --> 00:15:07.275
Jesus. what?

234
00:15:12.536 --> 00:15:15.826
So that's why we had
Charlie take Tyler home. Look...

235
00:15:16.832 --> 00:15:19.458
I don't think we have
much to worry about.

236
00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:20.460
Honestly.

237
00:15:21.462 --> 00:15:23.219
How do we know he told you the truth

238
00:15:23.221 --> 00:15:25.047
about what happened with the cops?

239
00:15:25.049 --> 00:15:26.673
Why would he lie?

240
00:15:26.675 --> 00:15:27.885
To save himself.

241
00:15:28.719 --> 00:15:32.137
Yeah. so I got him home
safe. He seemed pretty calm.

242
00:15:32.139 --> 00:15:33.805
How the fuck is he calm?

243
00:15:33.807 --> 00:15:36.892
Tyler doesn't want the truth
to come out any more than we do.

244
00:15:36.894 --> 00:15:39.645
He did the best he could with
the cops. All things considered.

245
00:15:39.647 --> 00:15:41.313
Let's say he's telling the truth.

246
00:15:41.315 --> 00:15:43.289
Just because he thinks
he fooled the cops

247
00:15:43.291 --> 00:15:44.858
doesn't mean he actually did.

248
00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:46.240
What if they're watching him now?

249
00:15:46.242 --> 00:15:47.653
What if they're watching all of us?

250
00:15:47.655 --> 00:15:49.237
That's what I don't get.

251
00:15:49.239 --> 00:15:51.406
Even if the cops didn't
believe Tyler about the guns.

252
00:15:51.408 --> 00:15:54.785
how does that lead them to
us or anything about Bryce?

253
00:15:54.787 --> 00:15:56.578
Tyler knows about Bryce.

254
00:15:56.580 --> 00:15:58.288
Tyler's in trouble for the guns.

255
00:15:58.290 --> 00:16:00.832
Tyler turns all of us
in to save himself.

256
00:16:00.834 --> 00:16:02.626
- He'd never do that.
- Are you sure?

257
00:16:02.628 --> 00:16:05.295
Tyler called Clay when he needed
help. I think we can trust him.

258
00:16:05.297 --> 00:16:08.590
Thanks. Cookies. but it's
not that fucking simple.

259
00:16:08.592 --> 00:16:11.176
Some of us are accessories
after the fact to murder.

260
00:16:11.178 --> 00:16:13.512
Hey. I planted evidence.
I'm an accessory.

261
00:16:13.514 --> 00:16:15.314
- We all are.
- Not me.

262
00:16:16.934 --> 00:16:19.726
Alex. you know Tyler wouldn't
want to hurt you. right?

263
00:16:19.728 --> 00:16:21.937
- Or any of us.
- With all due respect.

264
00:16:21.939 --> 00:16:23.814
you don't know him
well enough to say that.

265
00:16:23.816 --> 00:16:25.299
Actually. I feel like I do.

266
00:16:25.301 --> 00:16:27.635
I mean. us three. we've been
hanging out. like. every night.

267
00:16:27.637 --> 00:16:28.902
He's our friend.

268
00:16:28.904 --> 00:16:30.362
I believe Tyler.

269
00:16:30.364 --> 00:16:32.739
So does that mean that we do nothing?

270
00:16:32.741 --> 00:16:34.081
There's nothing we can do.

271
00:16:36.036 --> 00:16:37.076
So I say fuck it.

272
00:16:38.205 --> 00:16:39.788
Just let it play out.

273
00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:42.082
It's out of our hands.

274
00:16:42.084 --> 00:16:44.094
Jesus. Zach. dry out.

275
00:16:46.547 --> 00:16:48.257
Alex. you could talk to your dad.

276
00:16:49.174 --> 00:16:53.301
Get a feel for whether or not the
cops actually bought Tyler's story.

277
00:16:53.303 --> 00:16:55.804
- I could try.
- You guys. stop.

278
00:16:55.806 --> 00:16:57.848
We can't suddenly be going
around asking questions.

279
00:16:57.850 --> 00:16:59.350
Clay's right. we have to act normal.

280
00:17:00.227 --> 00:17:02.352
Everyone just needs to stay calm.

281
00:17:02.354 --> 00:17:05.355
keep their shit together.
and do not do anything stupid.

282
00:17:05.357 --> 00:17:08.777
Okay? Look. Ani and I.
we'll handle this.

283
00:17:11.196 --> 00:17:13.572
I wanted people to listen to me.

284
00:17:13.574 --> 00:17:14.906
Ever since Hannah and the tapes.

285
00:17:14.908 --> 00:17:17.118
I wanted people to wake
up and pay attention.

286
00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:20.037
Well. I guess I have
their attention now.

287
00:17:29.506 --> 00:17:31.089
- Hey.
- Hey.

288
00:17:31.091 --> 00:17:33.341
- Where's Clay?
- We have a new system.

289
00:17:33.343 --> 00:17:35.969
Kind of like a sock on
the door type of thing.

290
00:17:35.971 --> 00:17:38.271
So I can finally do this.

291
00:17:41.393 --> 00:17:43.560
- Jess. wait.
- Wait?

292
00:17:43.562 --> 00:17:46.021
What do you think I've been
doing for the last month?

293
00:17:46.023 --> 00:17:47.573
But I can't...

294
00:17:48.525 --> 00:17:49.525
do this. I...

295
00:17:53.781 --> 00:17:55.701
I can't be in a relationship.

296
00:17:56.867 --> 00:17:58.077
You're not serious.

297
00:17:59.745 --> 00:18:01.245
I have to make myself...

298
00:18:03.707 --> 00:18:04.707
my...

299
00:18:06.335 --> 00:18:07.495
my sobriety...

300
00:18:09.213 --> 00:18:11.171
the priority right now.

301
00:18:11.173 --> 00:18:13.465
It can be my priority too.

302
00:18:13.467 --> 00:18:16.426
I can help you. We can
figure this out together.

303
00:18:16.428 --> 00:18:17.758
It doesn't work like that.

304
00:18:18.597 --> 00:18:19.967
This. us...

305
00:18:21.433 --> 00:18:22.523
it's not good for me.

306
00:18:24.645 --> 00:18:27.521
- I'm not good for you?
- This isn't about you.

307
00:18:27.523 --> 00:18:30.113
- It's about me.
- Kind of always is. isn't it?

308
00:18:34.196 --> 00:18:35.356
I'm sorry.

309
00:18:39.535 --> 00:18:40.535
Okay.

310
00:18:43.831 --> 00:18:45.041
Merry Christmas.

311
00:19:04.017 --> 00:19:05.433
- Hey. Andy.
- Yeah?

312
00:19:05.435 --> 00:19:09.229
The Standall session with the Achola
girl the day before Thanksgiving.

313
00:19:09.231 --> 00:19:10.231
There's no tape.

314
00:19:11.024 --> 00:19:14.192
No. he didn't think anything
was gonna turn out. so...

315
00:19:14.194 --> 00:19:15.829
They were in there for five hours.

316
00:19:15.831 --> 00:19:17.988
He didn't turn on the camera? His phone?

317
00:19:19.783 --> 00:19:22.200
Just the written statement.
as far as I know.

318
00:19:22.202 --> 00:19:24.452
You want me to grab
Bill when he comes in?

319
00:19:24.454 --> 00:19:26.496
I mean. he's got a memory
like a fucking sponge.

320
00:19:26.498 --> 00:19:28.206
No. thank you. It's not important.

321
00:19:28.208 --> 00:19:31.209
I'll just... I'll pick his
brain when he comes in.

322
00:19:38.552 --> 00:19:40.051
Morning. buddy.

323
00:19:40.053 --> 00:19:41.970
Merry Christmas.

324
00:19:41.972 --> 00:19:44.556
You ready to come down
and. uh. open some presents?

325
00:19:44.558 --> 00:19:46.308
Yeah. sorry. I'll be right there.

326
00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:49.394
Just don't take too long. though.
Your mom made breakfast. Yeah.

327
00:19:49.396 --> 00:19:50.396
Hey. Dad?

328
00:19:51.481 --> 00:19:53.356
I heard about Tyler.

329
00:19:59.573 --> 00:20:00.573
What'd you hear?

330
00:20:01.742 --> 00:20:04.117
- He said everything was fine.
- And it is.

331
00:20:04.119 --> 00:20:06.119
Okay. that's not something
you have to worry about.

332
00:20:06.121 --> 00:20:08.171
You kids just keep
doing what you're doing.

333
00:20:08.999 --> 00:20:11.999
Let's just try to enjoy Christmas.
Can you do that for me?

334
00:20:16.173 --> 00:20:18.293
Winston. can we
please allow the maid in here?

335
00:20:19.092 --> 00:20:20.262
The dust is biblical.

336
00:20:22.888 --> 00:20:25.420
I get one private room
per the agreement.

337
00:20:25.422 --> 00:20:28.188
which you are currently
sort of violating.

338
00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:34.022
I heard back from my friend at Cho.

339
00:20:34.024 --> 00:20:36.942
They'll take you spring semester.
no questions asked.

340
00:20:36.944 --> 00:20:39.778
No questions except: "When
are you sending the check?"

341
00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:40.794
Right?

342
00:20:47.537 --> 00:20:49.621
I'll be fine going to Liberty.

343
00:20:49.623 --> 00:20:51.753
As public schools go. it's not the best.

344
00:20:53.502 --> 00:20:55.212
I know a few people there.

345
00:20:56.004 --> 00:20:57.974
It'll be nice to get closer to them.

346
00:21:06.098 --> 00:21:08.056
Holy shit!

347
00:21:08.058 --> 00:21:10.976
Sorry. but these are the brand-new ones!

348
00:21:10.978 --> 00:21:13.103
Pre-loaded with all the hot apps.

349
00:21:13.105 --> 00:21:15.313
I had a Mac Genius help me.

350
00:21:15.315 --> 00:21:16.975
Merry Christmas.

351
00:21:18.402 --> 00:21:21.945
Thank you. guys. Merry Christmas.

352
00:21:21.947 --> 00:21:24.030
You guys really went all-out.

353
00:21:24.032 --> 00:21:26.992
Well. it was Justin's
first holiday with us. so...

354
00:21:26.994 --> 00:21:29.452
And now we're broke. so
that's it till college.

355
00:21:29.454 --> 00:21:33.832
Actually. there is one more... thing.

356
00:21:33.834 --> 00:21:35.458
Honey. we were on a budget.

357
00:21:35.460 --> 00:21:39.090
Oh. I know. this is just
a little surprise. Go on.

358
00:21:48.348 --> 00:21:50.515
Oh. is this the picture
we took on Thanksgiving?

359
00:21:50.517 --> 00:21:53.347
Yeah. it turned out pretty good.
right? Given everything.

360
00:21:54.313 --> 00:21:55.653
Uh. I love it.

361
00:21:56.440 --> 00:21:59.274
As requested. a picture
of the four of us.

362
00:22:00.819 --> 00:22:03.029
Well. let's go find a place to put it.

363
00:22:09.244 --> 00:22:12.464
The truth is. this kind of thing
has been happening for a while.

364
00:22:15.208 --> 00:22:17.959
It started after Hannah
died. off and on.

365
00:22:17.961 --> 00:22:20.587
but then in the van on
the way to county jail.

366
00:22:20.589 --> 00:22:22.964
it was like this weight crushing me.

367
00:22:33.226 --> 00:22:34.768
Hey. you okay?

368
00:22:38.357 --> 00:22:39.857
Yeah. no. I'm fine. I. um...

369
00:22:40.984 --> 00:22:42.654
I think I just stood up too fast.

370
00:22:44.946 --> 00:22:46.654
It's like I can't breathe.

371
00:22:46.656 --> 00:22:50.158
like my heart's gonna beat out of
my chest. like... I'm gonna die.

372
00:22:56.541 --> 00:22:57.541
So...

373
00:22:58.835 --> 00:23:00.165
you should move in here.

374
00:23:00.962 --> 00:23:01.962
Sorry. uh...

375
00:23:02.714 --> 00:23:04.047
what?

376
00:23:04.049 --> 00:23:07.884
Well. my mom and my brothers
leave the day after tomorrow.

377
00:23:07.886 --> 00:23:11.888
Her job starts on the 28th.
so they're in Seattle for good.

378
00:23:11.890 --> 00:23:15.100
and my dad's transfer won't go
through for at least six months.

379
00:23:15.102 --> 00:23:16.482
so we're keeping the house.

380
00:23:17.813 --> 00:23:18.903
Empty bedroom.

381
00:23:20.023 --> 00:23:21.648
But I can't just move in.

382
00:23:21.650 --> 00:23:24.150
Oh. my dad would love to have you here.

383
00:23:25.195 --> 00:23:28.655
He thinks you're a good influence on me.

384
00:23:28.657 --> 00:23:30.737
Oh. well. that's sweet...

385
00:23:32.244 --> 00:23:33.414
... though misguided.

386
00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:37.414
Don't think my mother would approve.

387
00:23:37.416 --> 00:23:39.707
Well. you won't know
until you ask. right?

388
00:23:39.709 --> 00:23:40.839
I sort of think I do.

389
00:23:42.796 --> 00:23:44.256
Look. I don't have anyone.

390
00:23:45.966 --> 00:23:48.299
Come on. what would I do without you?

391
00:23:48.301 --> 00:23:49.591
I don't know. um...

392
00:23:50.554 --> 00:23:54.097
not strip naked at football
games or go to sex shops.

393
00:23:54.099 --> 00:23:55.269
Is this what you do?

394
00:23:56.309 --> 00:23:59.519
Just come in and save
everyone's lives and leave?

395
00:24:00.689 --> 00:24:03.689
Like you're some superhero
who's. like. above it all.

396
00:24:05.402 --> 00:24:06.734
No.

397
00:24:06.736 --> 00:24:07.736
I need you.

398
00:24:09.114 --> 00:24:10.244
Clay does.

399
00:24:11.408 --> 00:24:12.778
Ani. we all do.

400
00:24:18.874 --> 00:24:22.709
So you just talked. mostly. in rehab?

401
00:24:22.711 --> 00:24:26.713
Yeah. I mean. after all the
puking and the night sweats.

402
00:24:26.715 --> 00:24:28.585
Yeah. I remember it well.

403
00:24:31.595 --> 00:24:34.215
Yeah. we mostly just...
did a lot of talking.

404
00:24:35.515 --> 00:24:36.515
And. like...

405
00:24:37.309 --> 00:24:39.809
projects and hikes.

406
00:24:42.272 --> 00:24:45.732
Did you... talk about Bryce?

407
00:24:48.069 --> 00:24:49.199
Yeah. I mean. I...

408
00:24:50.822 --> 00:24:51.822
I had to.

409
00:24:52.824 --> 00:24:54.454
Just not about that.

410
00:24:56.828 --> 00:24:57.868
Just about the...

411
00:24:59.414 --> 00:25:00.834
the kind of person he was...

412
00:25:01.833 --> 00:25:02.833
to me.

413
00:25:05.128 --> 00:25:06.628
and him being gone. so...

414
00:25:17.766 --> 00:25:18.766
So the...

415
00:25:19.809 --> 00:25:20.889
the talking. it...

416
00:25:21.853 --> 00:25:22.936
it helped?

417
00:25:22.938 --> 00:25:23.938
I think so.

418
00:25:25.982 --> 00:25:26.982
I hope so.

419
00:25:29.611 --> 00:25:32.111
So. anyway. as I said.

420
00:25:32.113 --> 00:25:35.114
these boxes will be
gone in a couple of days.

421
00:25:35.116 --> 00:25:38.743
Then we can redecorate. whatever
the girls would like to do.

422
00:25:38.745 --> 00:25:40.453
We want it to feel like home.

423
00:25:40.455 --> 00:25:41.455
So. Mum?

424
00:25:42.666 --> 00:25:43.998
What do you think?

425
00:25:44.000 --> 00:25:45.959
I think it still feels very sudden.

426
00:25:45.961 --> 00:25:48.127
It is. but like we talked about.

427
00:25:48.129 --> 00:25:51.172
this way I can finish my senior
year at Liberty with my friends.

428
00:25:51.174 --> 00:25:53.800
and then I can come see
you on weekends. right?

429
00:25:53.802 --> 00:25:56.302
- You won't.
- Yes. I will!

430
00:25:56.304 --> 00:25:57.354
I promise.

431
00:26:01.643 --> 00:26:03.143
You have to check in daily.

432
00:26:04.229 --> 00:26:06.479
- Done.
- And she'll have a curfew?

433
00:26:06.481 --> 00:26:07.939
Oh. absolutely.

434
00:26:07.941 --> 00:26:09.901
Same as Jessica. Home by ten.

435
00:26:13.697 --> 00:26:14.697
Nine.

436
00:26:15.907 --> 00:26:17.156
Eight?

437
00:26:17.158 --> 00:26:18.616
Sundown.

438
00:26:18.618 --> 00:26:21.494
Colonel. I'll need your contact
details in case of emergency.

439
00:26:21.496 --> 00:26:22.616
Aye. aye. Captain.

440
00:26:25.667 --> 00:26:26.957
Just right this way.

441
00:26:31.047 --> 00:26:33.715
It'll be fucking great.
I'm so sick of boys.

442
00:26:33.717 --> 00:26:36.217
I mean. for me. You
and Clay. that's great.

443
00:26:36.219 --> 00:26:39.679
And now you don't have to do the
long-distance. Huge relief. right?

444
00:26:39.681 --> 00:26:41.514
No. right. that's...

445
00:26:41.516 --> 00:26:43.141
huge.

446
00:26:43.143 --> 00:26:46.023
You won't even have to tell
him that you were gonna leave.

447
00:26:46.855 --> 00:26:49.564
Sorry. um... where are we exactly?

448
00:26:49.566 --> 00:26:52.525
Oh. Dad used to take
us here for cookouts.

449
00:26:52.527 --> 00:26:55.987
And we're here now because...

450
00:26:55.989 --> 00:26:57.369
To deal with this.

451
00:26:59.743 --> 00:27:01.993
Is that Bryce's?

452
00:27:01.995 --> 00:27:04.155
Last remaining copy in the wild.

453
00:27:05.957 --> 00:27:08.708
Jess. what are you doing?

454
00:27:08.710 --> 00:27:09.710
Starting a fire.

455
00:27:13.173 --> 00:27:14.223
Are you sure?

456
00:27:15.550 --> 00:27:17.133
It's his last words.

457
00:27:17.135 --> 00:27:18.465
Did you want to hear them again?

458
00:27:19.262 --> 00:27:20.803
No.

459
00:27:20.805 --> 00:27:22.015
No. of course not.

460
00:27:44.788 --> 00:27:46.208
Toast? To Bryce?

461
00:27:47.248 --> 00:27:48.328
No. thank you.

462
00:27:53.838 --> 00:27:55.468
You wanted to leave. didn't you?

463
00:27:57.467 --> 00:27:59.634
To get away from all of this?

464
00:27:59.636 --> 00:28:01.676
I didn't want to.

465
00:28:04.015 --> 00:28:05.635
Then why didn't you tell anyone?

466
00:28:06.768 --> 00:28:07.768
I told you.

467
00:28:25.203 --> 00:28:26.543
Jess!

468
00:28:27.539 --> 00:28:29.249
Oh. fuck!

469
00:28:36.172 --> 00:28:37.172
- Hey.
- Hey.

470
00:28:40.135 --> 00:28:41.551
So. everything still good?

471
00:28:41.553 --> 00:28:42.635
With Tyler?

472
00:28:42.637 --> 00:28:44.247
Yeah. I spoke to
him every day over break.

473
00:28:44.249 --> 00:28:45.680
Story hasn't changed.

474
00:28:45.682 --> 00:28:47.982
What does Alex say? Does
his dad think that...

475
00:28:50.103 --> 00:28:51.894
What the hell?

476
00:28:58.069 --> 00:29:00.610
All right. Go ahead. step through.

477
00:29:00.612 --> 00:29:02.822
Backpacks on the table. please.

478
00:29:02.824 --> 00:29:04.454
What the actual fuck?

479
00:29:05.702 --> 00:29:07.952
- Keep coming.
- Don't lose your shit.

480
00:29:07.954 --> 00:29:10.246
Well. I haven't lost it yet. have I?

481
00:29:10.248 --> 00:29:12.957
Have your backpacks off.

482
00:29:12.959 --> 00:29:14.751
Your bag. please.

483
00:29:19.215 --> 00:29:20.425
Backpack on the table.

484
00:29:21.176 --> 00:29:22.176
Knock yourself out.

485
00:29:29.642 --> 00:29:31.235
Please step aside for a screening.

486
00:29:31.237 --> 00:29:33.652
It's probably the metal wire in my bra.

487
00:29:34.522 --> 00:29:36.189
We'll see.

488
00:29:36.191 --> 00:29:37.732
Step aside for a pat-down.

489
00:29:37.734 --> 00:29:40.234
I sure as shit hope you have
a female officer to do it.

490
00:29:40.236 --> 00:29:43.279
'cause you and your boys aren't
putting that anywhere near my body.

491
00:29:43.281 --> 00:29:44.947
Young lady.

492
00:29:44.949 --> 00:29:47.329
step aside now.

493
00:29:49.829 --> 00:29:51.287
Whatever.

494
00:29:51.289 --> 00:29:52.789
Hey! Get back here!

495
00:29:58.171 --> 00:30:00.588
Think it's a coincidence the
school installed metal detectors

496
00:30:00.590 --> 00:30:03.049
less than two weeks after
the cops talked to Tyler?

497
00:30:03.051 --> 00:30:06.141
Bureaucracies don't move
that fast. like. ever.

498
00:30:07.263 --> 00:30:09.096
They know. They have to know.

499
00:30:09.098 --> 00:30:11.349
Yeah. or the school's
just covering its arse

500
00:30:11.351 --> 00:30:14.644
after being ground zero for a
high-profile murder investigation.

501
00:30:17.690 --> 00:30:19.150
Just take your own advice:

502
00:30:20.193 --> 00:30:21.993
stay calm.

503
00:30:28.952 --> 00:30:30.622
I'm not gonna apologize.

504
00:30:31.496 --> 00:30:34.497
If you're gonna turn Liberty
into a full-on police state.

505
00:30:34.499 --> 00:30:36.207
then at least show
your female students...

506
00:30:36.209 --> 00:30:37.458
Police state's a strong word.

507
00:30:37.460 --> 00:30:40.086
Then at least show your
female students some respect

508
00:30:40.088 --> 00:30:44.771
by hiring actual female officers
to do the so-called screenings.

509
00:30:44.773 --> 00:30:46.653
You're absolutely right. Ms. Davis.

510
00:30:47.637 --> 00:30:49.807
Uh... you have my sincere apology.

511
00:30:50.640 --> 00:30:52.056
- I do?
- And moving forward.

512
00:30:52.058 --> 00:30:55.643
I'd love to get your input as we
implement these new measures.

513
00:30:55.645 --> 00:30:57.520
You're trying to keep me quiet.

514
00:30:57.522 --> 00:31:00.731
Oh. when have I ever been
able to keep you quiet?

515
00:31:00.733 --> 00:31:03.359
Look. we want the same thing.

516
00:31:03.361 --> 00:31:05.991
To make kids feel safe. to protect them.

517
00:31:07.782 --> 00:31:09.490
You believe me. don't you?

518
00:31:09.492 --> 00:31:12.034
- I guess.
- Then will you help me?

519
00:31:12.036 --> 00:31:13.327
Help you how?

520
00:31:13.329 --> 00:31:15.079
Tell me the truth in confidence.

521
00:31:15.081 --> 00:31:17.123
and if there's anything
that you're worried about.

522
00:31:17.125 --> 00:31:19.915
if you see anything going on.

523
00:31:20.837 --> 00:31:21.917
you come to me first.

524
00:31:25.383 --> 00:31:26.674
The future fair.

525
00:31:26.676 --> 00:31:28.384
They changed it from college fair

526
00:31:28.386 --> 00:31:29.740
because there's this new thing

527
00:31:29.742 --> 00:31:31.721
that not all kids should go to college.

528
00:31:31.723 --> 00:31:34.082
and they threw in. like.
clubs and firemen

529
00:31:34.084 --> 00:31:35.850
just so no one felt left out.

530
00:31:35.852 --> 00:31:38.772
Look. it's all a fucking joke.
This planet has no future.

531
00:31:39.564 --> 00:31:42.398
So Bolan didn't reprimand you?

532
00:31:42.400 --> 00:31:44.567
He just wanted a chat?

533
00:31:44.569 --> 00:31:46.694
Crazy. right?

534
00:31:46.696 --> 00:31:51.115
What. and he didn't ask you
for anything or to do anything?

535
00:31:51.117 --> 00:31:52.700
Or not do?

536
00:31:52.702 --> 00:31:54.076
No.

537
00:31:54.078 --> 00:31:55.078
Nothing.

538
00:31:56.497 --> 00:31:58.164
Good turnout this year. right?

539
00:31:58.166 --> 00:31:59.326
Is it?

540
00:32:06.132 --> 00:32:07.132
I. uh...

541
00:32:10.970 --> 00:32:12.060
I'll be right back.

542
00:32:12.847 --> 00:32:14.555
Where are you going?

543
00:32:14.557 --> 00:32:15.557
Ani!

544
00:32:18.311 --> 00:32:20.731
Hi. um. I'm Estella.

545
00:32:23.274 --> 00:32:24.404
I know who you are.

546
00:32:25.818 --> 00:32:26.818
Sorry.

547
00:32:30.406 --> 00:32:31.406
Sorry.

548
00:32:32.575 --> 00:32:35.285
I just wanted to say I really
admire what you're doing.

549
00:32:36.412 --> 00:32:38.622
Trying to change the
culture of the school?

550
00:32:39.832 --> 00:32:42.249
Oh... thanks.

551
00:32:42.251 --> 00:32:44.175
