599
00:35:29.627 --> 00:35:30.627
What's that?

600
00:35:31.879 --> 00:35:34.589
Uh... It's... Dr. Singh.

601
00:35:35.591 --> 00:35:38.759
Guess she heard that
there's an admissions officer

602
00:35:38.761 --> 00:35:40.101
that was interested in me?

603
00:35:41.848 --> 00:35:42.848
At Occidental?

604
00:35:44.142 --> 00:35:45.312
They liked my essay.

605
00:35:46.561 --> 00:35:49.436
I guess if you have.
like. life circumstances

606
00:35:49.438 --> 00:35:51.478
and a good story or whatever.

607
00:35:55.361 --> 00:35:58.031
Anyway. it's not like
I'm gonna get in. so...

608
00:35:58.906 --> 00:35:59.946
don't worry.

609
00:36:00.783 --> 00:36:01.913
Why would I worry?

610
00:36:03.035 --> 00:36:05.155
You should go if you can.
it's a great school.

611
00:36:09.417 --> 00:36:11.377
What do you mean you go here now?

612
00:36:12.753 --> 00:36:14.295
I transferred.

613
00:36:14.297 --> 00:36:15.297
Why?

614
00:36:16.716 --> 00:36:18.215
I got expelled.

615
00:36:18.217 --> 00:36:21.093
That kid Bryan Chu got caught
hacking the school servers

616
00:36:21.095 --> 00:36:24.015
and ratted us all out to save
his sorry little ass. so...

617
00:36:24.974 --> 00:36:27.854
bye-bye. Hillcrest and Princeton.

618
00:36:29.045 --> 00:36:30.060
Shit.

619
00:36:30.062 --> 00:36:32.813
It's kind of a relief.
really. Getting caught.

620
00:36:32.815 --> 00:36:35.185
I don't have to live with
that secret anymore. you know?

621
00:36:36.903 --> 00:36:38.073
That shit can kill you.

622
00:36:39.655 --> 00:36:43.235
Besides. I think it's
growing on me. Liberty.

623
00:36:45.536 --> 00:36:47.826
I think I could make a
future for myself here.

624
00:36:53.085 --> 00:36:54.752
We can contain this.

625
00:36:54.754 --> 00:36:56.804
Nobody here even knows who Winston is.

626
00:36:57.757 --> 00:36:58.797
Except Alex.

627
00:36:58.799 --> 00:37:00.719
Who we absolutely shouldn't tell.

628
00:37:01.552 --> 00:37:02.552
I don't get it.

629
00:37:03.429 --> 00:37:06.847
Monty beat the shit out of him.
Why would Winston go back?

630
00:37:06.849 --> 00:37:08.400
Fuck if I know.

631
00:37:08.402 --> 00:37:10.112
Why would Jess go back with Justin?

632
00:37:11.395 --> 00:37:13.896
All I know is that they
were together that night.

633
00:37:13.898 --> 00:37:15.895
So then. why hasn't
he done anything yet?

634
00:37:15.897 --> 00:37:18.067
Why aren't we all in jail already?

635
00:37:18.069 --> 00:37:19.699
Maybe he doesn't have any proof.

636
00:37:21.030 --> 00:37:22.450
Maybe that's why he's here.

637
00:37:24.116 --> 00:37:25.446
To get proof.

638
00:37:27.912 --> 00:37:29.718
And you said everything was handled.

639
00:37:29.720 --> 00:37:32.081
You said that Tyler's guns were handled.

640
00:37:32.083 --> 00:37:33.123
They are.

641
00:37:33.125 --> 00:37:35.940
But you don't really
believe that. do you?

642
00:37:35.942 --> 00:37:38.611
You knew about this since Thanksgiving.
and you're telling me now?

643
00:37:38.613 --> 00:37:40.030
I was hoping it would go away.

644
00:37:40.032 --> 00:37:42.675
Why didn't you tell me you
were moving to Oakland?

645
00:37:42.677 --> 00:37:44.511
What the fuck? Why don't
you tell me anything?

646
00:37:44.513 --> 00:37:48.013
Because you were falling apart.
Because you were a fucking mess.

647
00:37:52.103 --> 00:37:53.811
Well. I'm fine now.

648
00:37:53.813 --> 00:37:54.813
I'm fine.

649
00:37:57.525 --> 00:37:58.525
Clay.

650
00:38:07.743 --> 00:38:08.793
I. um...

651
00:38:09.755 --> 00:38:10.786
I gotta...

652
00:38:10.788 --> 00:38:11.788
Clay!

653
00:38:38.691 --> 00:38:40.231
We had 'em made for today.

654
00:38:43.321 --> 00:38:46.447
- Thanks.
- No. you gotta put it on.

655
00:38:46.449 --> 00:38:48.324
- Maybe later.
- Come on. Estella.

656
00:38:48.326 --> 00:38:50.906
You gotta wear it. It's the
only tribute he's gonna get.

657
00:38:52.913 --> 00:38:54.213
It's sweet. guys. but...

658
00:38:55.082 --> 00:38:58.250
- I'm just gonna wear it at home.
- No. you gotta wear it now.

659
00:38:58.252 --> 00:38:59.252
It's for today.

660
00:39:02.423 --> 00:39:04.923
Come on. guys. she
doesn't want to wear it.

661
00:39:04.925 --> 00:39:07.468
Of course she wants to
wear it. It's her brother.

662
00:39:07.470 --> 00:39:09.345
Unlike you. she's sad that he's dead.

663
00:39:09.347 --> 00:39:11.680
Yeah. I'm sure she is.

664
00:39:11.682 --> 00:39:14.767
but I don't think you
get to say how she feels.

665
00:39:14.769 --> 00:39:15.769
Or how I feel.

666
00:39:16.604 --> 00:39:18.314
So. maybe back off.

667
00:39:21.192 --> 00:39:22.775
That's right.

668
00:39:22.777 --> 00:39:23.897
She's my sister.

669
00:39:30.910 --> 00:39:32.242
Now back off.

670
00:39:32.244 --> 00:39:33.254
All you guys.

671
00:39:35.539 --> 00:39:36.789
Or what?

672
00:39:44.632 --> 00:39:48.092
Fucking take those jerseys off.
You're honoring a fucking rapist.

673
00:39:48.094 --> 00:39:50.719
Fuck you. Jensen. He took
the fall for you. man.

674
00:39:50.721 --> 00:39:52.101
No way did he kill Bryce.

675
00:39:52.890 --> 00:39:54.060
Everyone knows that.

676
00:39:56.435 --> 00:39:57.435
Bullshit!

677
00:39:58.396 --> 00:39:59.936
You're the real criminal.

678
00:40:03.609 --> 00:40:06.193
What the fuck are you doing?

679
00:40:14.662 --> 00:40:16.042
Get the fuck off me!

680
00:40:29.927 --> 00:40:31.637
So much for staying calm.

681
00:40:36.475 --> 00:40:38.308
SROs think they started it.

682
00:40:38.310 --> 00:40:40.102
They're getting detention. not me.

683
00:40:40.104 --> 00:40:41.437
Oh. that's lovely.

684
00:40:41.439 --> 00:40:43.819
What happened to not
doing anything stupid?

685
00:40:45.025 --> 00:40:47.401
You heard what they were saying.

686
00:40:47.403 --> 00:40:50.154
that he was innocent. that
we covered up Bryce's murder.

687
00:40:50.156 --> 00:40:52.531
- What if they know?
- They're just making things up

688
00:40:52.533 --> 00:40:54.953
'cause they don't want to
believe Monty would kill Bryce.

689
00:40:58.038 --> 00:40:59.038
Clay...

690
00:41:01.083 --> 00:41:02.083
what happened?

691
00:41:03.836 --> 00:41:05.544
Even before the fight...

692
00:41:05.546 --> 00:41:07.666
you... went away.

693
00:41:09.049 --> 00:41:10.049
Where?

694
00:41:12.845 --> 00:41:15.679
So basically. the darkroom
is first come. first served.

695
00:41:15.681 --> 00:41:19.433
Um... unless you're on a deadline.
and then you get priority.

696
00:41:19.435 --> 00:41:21.225
- So...
- Dude. these are really good.

697
00:41:22.438 --> 00:41:23.858
For a yearbook layout. or...

698
00:41:25.733 --> 00:41:26.783
student leaders?

699
00:41:27.818 --> 00:41:28.858
No. uh...

700
00:41:30.321 --> 00:41:32.531
those are for a thing
I did with my friends.

701
00:41:33.866 --> 00:41:34.866
For an exhibit.

702
00:41:36.410 --> 00:41:38.785
You're friends with Ani and Clay?

703
00:41:38.787 --> 00:41:40.078
Yeah.

704
00:41:40.080 --> 00:41:41.371
Wait. do you know them?

705
00:41:41.373 --> 00:41:43.343
Uh... sort of.

706
00:41:43.345 --> 00:41:44.909
Ani showed me around the future fair.

707
00:41:44.911 --> 00:41:48.295
and I saw Clay on
the news last semester.

708
00:41:48.297 --> 00:41:50.631
Okay. well. don't believe the news.

709
00:41:50.633 --> 00:41:53.467
'cause Clay's a really great guy.

710
00:41:53.469 --> 00:41:55.969
I mean. he's always been there for me.

711
00:41:55.971 --> 00:41:56.971
and Ani too.

712
00:42:01.101 --> 00:42:03.519
Hey. could I borrow the last
couple of years' yearbooks?

713
00:42:03.521 --> 00:42:05.979
